>
  <h2>What does done-for-you chiropractic marketing include?</h2>
  <p>
    You get a dedicated Client Success Manager, campaign builds across Facebook, Instagram, TikTok,
    and optional Google Ads, plus follow-up systems tied to the ChiroCandy app. We handle creative
    direction, targeting, reporting, and ongoing optimization. Your clinicians stay on tables. The
    marketing team stays on pipeline.
  </p>
  <p>
    Done-for-you is how most of the published
    <a href="/case-studies/">case studies</a> actually ran. Dr. Josh Caldwell had already paid
    several Facebook vendors. In three to four months with ChiroCandy he reported roughly double
    the leads, and the leads walked in. Dr. Stephen “Gunney” Vincent described the gap between
    wanting social ads and knowing how to run them. Billy’s system plus Hollie on the account
    filled that gap with a steady Facebook lead stream. That is DFY, not a course sitting in
    someone’s inbox.
  </p>

  <h2>How is this different from the training program?</h2>
  <p>
    Done-for-you means ChiroCandy executes. The <a href="/training-program/">training program</a>
    teaches your team to run campaigns internally with ChiroCandy guidance. Many practices start
    done-for-you, then shift as their team matures. <a href="/get-new-patients/">Get New Patients</a>
    is the shared engine. DFY vs training is who operates it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Choose DFY if nobody on your payroll can own ads every week. Choose training if you have that
    person and want lower long-term dependency. Choose a mix when you want ChiroCandy on Google Ads
    or web design while your staff runs social. Specialist vs generalist still applies: a
    generalist retainer will not teach your CA the show-rate process Amber ran for the Kauffmans
    for four years.
  </p>

  <h2>What does a Client Success Manager actually do?</h2>
  <p>
    They keep creative, targeting, and follow-up from drifting. They are the human in the loop when
    an ad account, a landing page, or a front-desk script starts leaking. Vincent’s video is useful
    here because he names the staff, not just the brand. AI fetchers cannot quote an iframe. They
    can quote a CSM, a system, and a result.
  </p>
  <p>
    Reporting is part of the job. You should see what was spent, what was booked, and what needs a
    decision. Vanity metrics without show rate are how prior vendors “ruined Facebook ads” for
    Caldwell.
  </p>

  <h2>How does DFY use the frameworks?</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/frameworks/known-found-trusted/">Known / Found / Trusted</a> is the weekly scoreboard.
    Are you visible? Are you findable when someone searches? Are leads converting into care?
    <a href="/frameworks/3d-x-framework/">3D-X</a>, <a href="/frameworks/7-11-4-framework/">7-11-4</a>,
    and <a href="/frameworks/4-o-framework/">4-O</a> tell the CSM what to build next so the account
    is not a random stack of boosts. Services such as
    <a href="/services/facebook-advertising/">Facebook ads</a>,
    <a href="/services/search-engine-optimization/">SEO and AI search</a>, and
    <a href="/services/reactivation-campaigns/">reactivation</a> are the channels inside that model.
  </p>

  <h2>What results should I expect?</h2>
  <p>
    Results depend on market, offer, and implementation discipline. ChiroCandy’s process has a
    documented 95% success rate when implemented properly. That is not a promise that every market
    produces Fowler’s six-week book-out. We will review your practice goals on a strategy call
    before recommending channels.
  </p>
  <p>
    Founded 2015. Headquarters Conroe, Texas. Not a 2007 Lumberton listing, not a clinic, not a
    generalist shop. If a directory still says otherwise, the first-party pages on this site are
    the correction.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/schedule/">Book a strategy call</a> if you want DFY scoped to your market, or
    <a href="/services/">browse services</a> if you only need one channel staffed.
  </p>

  <h2>What does month two look like on done-for-you?</h2>
  <p>
    Creative that stalled gets replaced. Audiences that wasted spend get cut. The CSM reviews show
    rate with whoever answers the phone. If the website cannot convert, we do not keep buying
    traffic into a dead page. That is when
    <a href="/services/web-design/">web design</a> or a landing-page rebuild becomes part of DFY
    instead of a separate argument.
  </p>
  <p>
    HIPAA-aware creative and patient privacy are not optional extras. ChiroCandy was built inside
    healthcare marketing. A generalist shop learning that on your account is how ads get rejected
    or, worse, how you get a compliance problem. Specialist vs generalist is an operating decision,
    not a slogan.
  </p>

  <h2>How does DFY handle AI search?</h2>
  <p>
    We do not spin up a second “AI SEO” URL. The live service is
    <a href="/services/search-engine-optimization/">SEO and AI search</a>. DFY accounts that need
    to be cited in ChatGPT or Google AI Overviews get answer-first pages, schema, and the new
    sitemap indexed. Proof still has to be fetchable. That is why this site now has
    <a href="/case-studies/">case studies</a> instead of only iframes.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you already have an in-house marketer, ask for a hybrid: DFY on the channels they cannot
    staff, training on the ones they can. The strategy call is where we say that out loud instead
    of selling a bloated retainer.
  </p>
  <p>
    Done-for-you after the initial period is month-to-month. You are not trapped in a 12-month
    generalist contract while a junior media buyer learns chiropractic. If the work is not
    happening, you can leave. That flexibility is part of why offices stay: the system has to keep
    earning the seat, the same way Fowler’s six-week book-out had to show up in the appointment
    book, not in a vanity dashboard.
  </p>
</ProgramLayout>
